## Metadata
Title: FUN'S Cross-Word Puzzles
Author: Evangeline Kearney
Copyright: New York World
Date: 1914-03-08
Number: 12
Description: A 13-wide diamond with a shaded cross in the centre carrying the printed number (shown as _), the same template as No. 11.
Source: Milwaukee Sentinel, 1914-03-08, p. 82
Solution-Source: Milwaukee Sentinel, 1914-03-15, p. 86


## Printed
heading: FUN'S CROSS-WORD PUZZLES
heading (left of grid): Can You
heading (right of grid): Solve Them?
number: No 12
credit: Today's cross work puzzle, the twelfth in FUN'S series, was sent in by Miss Evangeline Kearney of 207 Winthrop street, Brooklyn.
instructions: See if you can solve it. Fill in the small squares in the above diamond with words corresponding to the clews and definitions given below. On another page you will find the solutions of last week's puzzle. The solution to today's puzzle will be given in next week's FUN.
solution heading: SOLUTION TO No 12 PUZZLE
solution caption: So many FUN puzzle solvers are sending in cross word puzzle, made by themselves with a request that they be published, that the puzzle editor is beginning to wonder what to do with them all. Those puzzles which are available will be published as early as possible. The
solution caption (continued): solution to last week's cross word puzzle is given herewith. Today's cross work puzzle is more difficult than last week's.


